{"test_cases_lookup_map": {"{\"actual_output\": null, \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": \"Employees may take sick leave when they are unable to work due to illness according to the company's sick leave policy.\", \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"What is the sick leave policy?\", \"retrieval_context\": [\"Cancellation is subject to operational requirements and manager approval.\\n\\nLeave Records\\n\\nEmployees are responsible for reviewing their leave balances and ensuring that submitted requests contain accurate dates and information.\\n\\nThe company maintains official leave records through its designated HR system.\\n\\nPolicy Compliance\\n\\nEmployees are expected to follow this policy and any applicable employment laws and local regulations.\\n\\nThe company reserves the right to update this policy when business or legal requirements change.\", \"EXPENSE POLICY\\n\\nPurpose\\n\\nThis policy defines the rules for submitting, approving, and reimbursing legitimate business expenses incurred by employees.\\n\\nEligible Expenses\\n\\nReasonable and necessary expenses incurred for legitimate business purposes may be reimbursable.\\n\\nExamples include:\\n\\nBusiness travel\\nTransportation\\nAccommodation\\nBusiness meals\\nClient or business meetings\\nApproved conferences and events\\nOther expenses specifically authorized by the company\\nPrior Approval\\n\\nEmployees should obtain manager approval before incurring significant or unusual business expenses.\\n\\nTravel and other expenses that exceed department-approved limits may require additional authorization.\\n\\nBusiness Travel\\n\\nEmployees should use reasonable and cost-effective transportation and accommodation options.\\n\\nWhen booking travel, employees should use company-approved travel providers when available.\", \"LEAVE POLICY\\n\\nPurpose\\n\\nThis policy defines the rules and procedures for requesting, approving, and managing employee leave.\\n\\nTypes of Leave\\n\\nEmployees may request the following types of leave:\\n\\nAnnual Leave: Paid time off for personal or vacation purposes.\\nSick Leave: Leave taken when an employee is ill or requires medical attention.\\nEmergency Leave: Short-notice leave required due to an unexpected personal or family emergency.\\nBereavement Leave: Leave provided following the death of an immediate family member.\\nUnpaid Leave: Leave that may be approved when an employee has exhausted applicable paid leave or requires an extended absence.\\nAnnual Leave\\n\\nEmployees should submit annual leave requests at least 3 working days before the intended start date.\\n\\nAnnual leave is subject to manager approval and business requirements.\\n\\nEmployees should avoid scheduling leave during critical project deadlines unless prior approval has been obtained.\\n\\nSick Leave\", \"REMOTE WORK POLICY\\n\\nPurpose\\n\\nThis policy establishes guidelines for employees who work remotely or use a hybrid work arrangement.\\n\\nEligibility\\n\\nRemote work eligibility depends on:\\n\\nJob responsibilities\\nTeam requirements\\nBusiness needs\\nManager approval\\nEmployee performance and reliability\\n\\nNot all roles are suitable for remote work.\\n\\nWorking Hours\\n\\nEmployees working remotely are expected to maintain their agreed working schedule and remain available during required core working hours.\\n\\nEmployees should communicate any significant changes to their availability with their manager.\\n\\nAvailability and Communication\\n\\nEmployees must remain reachable through approved company communication channels during working hours.\\n\\nEmployees are expected to:\\n\\nAttend scheduled meetings.\\nRespond to important messages within a reasonable timeframe.\\nKeep their calendar and availability reasonably up to date.\\nInform their manager of extended periods of unavailability.\\nWork Environment\", \"Sick Leave\\n\\nEmployees should notify their manager as soon as reasonably possible when they are unable to work due